{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794937400","published":"2026-11-17T17:43:40Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:28:41.026490904Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-109269","CVE-2026-116147","CVE-2026-116159","CVE-2026-61868","CVE-2026-61869"],"summary":"Fix of 14 CVEs","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: information disclosure in the JPEG decoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-109269.patch: only report the sampling factors\n       of the components present in the image in\n       JPEGSetImageSamplingFactor() in coders/jpeg.c\n     - CVE-2026-109269\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak in the MIFF encoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-61869.patch: destroy the quantum info when a\n       memory allocation fails in WriteMIFFImage() in coders/miff.c\n     - CVE-2026-61869\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak in the YUV decoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-61868.patch: release the chroma image on the\n       error paths in ReadYUVImage() in coders/yuv.c\n     - CVE-2026-61868\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: NULL pointer dereference in the DJVU decoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116147.patch: check the result of\n       CloneImageList() in ReadDJVUImage() in coders/djvu.c\n     - CVE-2026-116147\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak of the -cdl option\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116159.patch: free the color correction\n       collection in MogrifyImage() in wand/mogrify.c\n     - CVE-2026-116159","affected":[{"package":{"name":"imagemagick","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:18.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/imagemagick?distro=ubuntu-18.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8:6.9.7.4+dfsg-16ubuntu6.15+tuxcare.els57"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu18.04els/CLSA-2026-1794937400.json"}},{"package":{"name":"imagemagick-6-common","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:18.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/imagemagick-6-common?distro=ubuntu-18.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"f